meta {
  name: Permanently block (hotlist) a fuel card
  type: http
  seq: 120
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/fuel-cards/{{plutusApiFuelCardId}}/permanent-block?reason=Driver left the organisation
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  reason: Driver left the organisation
  ~transferToCardId: {{plutusApiFuelCardTransferToId}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  `PUT /api/fuel-cards/{id}/permanent-block`: the closest thing plutus-api has to deleting a BPCL card.
  BPCL has no delete; this hotlists the card at the provider and marks our row `CLOSED` with the reason.
  It cannot be undone. Run it on purpose, one card at a time, and never against a production card from here.

  plutus-java: `FuelCardResource.permanentBlockFuelCard` -> `FuelCardService.permanentBlockCard` ->
  `BPCLClient.permanentBlockCard` (BPCL change-status `hotlist`, success is a 202 from BPCL).

  Inputs:
  - `plutusApiFuelCardId`: our `fuel_cards.id`, not the card number.
  - `reason` (optional): saved as the block reason.
  - `transferToCardId` (optional, disabled here): an ACTIVE card of the same provider. Required when the
    card still has a balance, which is moved there before the hotlist. Enable it and set
    `plutusApiFuelCardTransferToId` for that case.

  Roles: VAHN_ADMIN, TORG_ADMIN, TRUCK_MANAGER, FUND_MANAGER, ACCOUNTANT, OPERATOR.

  Responses:
  - 200 with an empty body: hotlisted, row is now `CLOSED`.
  - 400 "Fuel card balance is not zero": pass `transferToCardId`.
  - 400 "Fuel card is not active": already blocked or closed.
  - 503 "Unable to permanently block fuel card": BPCL refused or the balance transfer failed.

  Watch out:
  - The torg ownership check is commented out in the service, so any of the roles above can hotlist any
    card id, including another torg's.
  - The phone number is not unassigned at BPCL first (BPCL asked for unassign before hotlist, and
    `BPCLClient` has no `unassignDriver`). Creating a new BPCL card for the same mobile number may still
    fail until the number is unassigned on the BPCL web portal.
}
